# {{proper_name}}

This app was created using the Tethys + Next.js app scaffold. It uses Next.js (as a static export) for the frontend of the app and Tethys as the backend.

## Development Installation

You need to install both the Tethys dependencies and the node dependencies:

1. Install the app in Tethys Platform

```
conda activate tethys
cd tethysapp-{{project}}
tethys install -d
```

2. Install the node dependencies

```
cd tethysapp-{{project}}
npm install
```

## Development

The Next.js dev server is configured to forward any route it does not handle to the Tethys development server (see `next.config.mjs`). Start both in separate terminals.

1. Start Tethys development server

```
tethys manage start
```

2. Start the Next.js development server (in separate terminal)

```
npm run dev
```

Then open http://localhost:3000/apps/{{project_url}}/

### Logging in during development

Log in at http://localhost:8000/accounts/login/, on the Tethys server. Django rejects logins sent through the Next.js dev server on port 3000.

Use `localhost` in both addresses, not `127.0.0.1`. Browsers keep logins per hostname, so a login on `127.0.0.1:8000` is not seen by `localhost:3000`.

### Port 8000 or 3000

http://localhost:8000/apps/{{project_url}}/ serves the output of the last `npm run build`, so it does not change when you edit files. Use port 3000 while developing, and run `npm run build` again to update the port 8000 version.

## Build

Next.js is configured to export the app as static files and copy them into the `tethysapp/{{project}}/public/frontend` directory. Before building a Python distribution for release, run:

```
npm run build
```